INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_OM_REPO_TEXT="%s\n\nPackage <b>conky</b> is located in <tt>rolling-x86_64-extra</tt> repository.\nTo receive updates, it is recommended to enable it in system settings.\n\nWhat do you want to do?"
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_OM_TEMP_WARN="ℹ️ <b>Temporary installation mode selected.</b>\n\nScript will force installation of package <b>conky</b> using repository <tt>rolling-x86_64-extra</tt> <b>only once</b>.\n\n⚠️ <b>System configuration will not be changed permanently.</b>\nThis means conky package will install correctly, but system might not detect updates automatically in future.\n\nDo you want to continue?"
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_OM_ROCK_WARN="⚠️ <big><b>Stable OpenMandriva (Rock) version detected.</b></big>\n\nFor widget to work correctly, installer will download newer version of package <tt>conky</tt> (with Lua/Cairo support) using <b>Rolling</b> repository.\n\nDo you agree to temporarily download package from newer system?\n(This won't affect stability of rest of the system)."
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_OM_REFRESHING="🔄 <b>Refreshing package database...</b>\n\nPlease wait, checking changes."
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_OM_VERIFYING="🔍 Verifying..."

# Packages and Installation (Main loop)
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_MANUAL_TEXT="<big><b>Emergency mode: manual installation.</b></big>\n\nMissing packages:\n<b><tt>%s</tt></b>\n\nRun the following command in terminal:\n<b><tt>%s</tt></b>\n\nClick <b>Open terminal</b> to open blank terminal.\nAfter installation click <b>OK</b>, and script will check dependencies."
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_SKIP_WARN="<big>⚠️ <b>Are you sure you want to skip dependency check?</b></big>\n\n<span foreground='red'>Skipping this step means script won't verify if required packages (Conky, Lua, Wget etc.) are installed.</span>\n\nIf they are missing, widget won't start correctly or errors will occur.\n\nAre you aware of risk and want to continue?"
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_UNKNOWN_HEADER="<span foreground='red'><big><big><b>Package manager not recognized!</b></big></big></span>"
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_UNKNOWN_TEXT="<big><big>🖥️ OS: <b>%s</b> | Version: <b>%s</b></big></big>\n\n%s\n\nScript has no automatic installation rules for this system.\nYou must manually install following packages:\n\n<tt>%s</tt>\n\n• <b>Don't check dependencies</b> - Click to skip system package verification and proceed to Python venv configuration.\n• <b>Cancel</b> – Terminate script."
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_MISSING_HEADER="🔧 <big><b>The following packages must be installed in system:</b></big>"
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_MISSING_HEADER_AGAIN="<span foreground='red'>🔧 <big><big><b>The following packages are still missing in system!</b></big></big></span>"
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_MISSING_TEXT="<big><big>🖥️ OS: <b>%s</b> | Version: <b>%s</b></big></big>\n\n%s\n\n<b><tt>%s</tt></b>\n\n• <b>Installation</b> - Click for script to guide you through automatic installation of needed dependencies.\n• <b>Everything OK</b> - Click if dependencies were installed successfully. Script will check validity.\n• <b>Safe mode</b> - Click in case of problems with automatic installation. You will get command to execute manually in terminal.\n• <b>Cancel</b> – terminates script."
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES_AUTO_INSTALL_TEXT="<big><b>Automatic installation started in terminal.\nIf needed, type sudo password.</b></big>\n\nMissing dependencies (installing):\n<b><tt>%s</tt></b>\n\nAfter installation finishes in terminal click <b>Everything OK</b> to check again.\nIf you encounter problem, use <b>Safe mode</b>."

